================================================================================
PaiNN Debiasing & Cross-Molecule Generalization Supplemental Experiment
Addressing Final Review Recommendation #5 (终审建议第5项)
================================================================================
Objective:
  Phase A - Uracil independent multi-seed validation (eliminate single-seed luck)
  Phase B - Zero-tuning cross-molecule generalization test (eliminate architecture-
            selection bias)

Protocol provenance (identical to protected optimized_code/painn/eval_benchmark.py):
  cutoff=5.0, n_atom_basis=128, n_interactions=3, batch_size=32, epochs=80
  AdamW(lr=1e-3, weight_decay=0.0), CosineAnnealingLR(T_max=80, eta_min=1e-5)
  loss = 0.01*MSE_E + 0.99*MSE_F, grad_clip max_norm=10.0
  Validation every 5 epochs on val Force MAE; best checkpoint kept in memory;
  single final test-set evaluation at the end.

Architecture provenance:
  "improved" = current HEAD of optimized_code/painn (git tag _best = c5c1199498,
      iter-7 tanh-gate PaiNN: bidirectional qi/qj message + 3-body geometric
      gating + tanh gate), code at optimized_code/painn/src (UNMODIFIED).
  "baseline" = original PaiNNInteraction/PaiNNMixing at git tag _baseline,
      isolated into scripts/painn_generalization/baseline_src (verified
      byte-for-byte identical to the _baseline tag; diff-confirmed to differ
      from the improved HEAD only in painn.py).
  Both architectures run via scripts/painn_generalization/run_experiment.py,
  a thin parameterized wrapper that reproduces eval_benchmark.py's protocol
  line-for-line (protected eval_benchmark.py and data/md17_uracil_split.npz
  are NEVER modified).

Hardware disclosure:
  nvidia-smi and torch.cuda.is_available() both confirm NO GPU is present in
  this execution environment, contradicting the premise of "current GPU" in
  the task description. ALL runs below execute on CPU only
  (/home/ymujdb/miniconda3/envs/cgcnn_env, 24 logical cores, 4 threads/run,
  up to 6 runs executed concurrently).

Phase A molecule/split: Uracil, data/md17_uracil_split.npz (PROTECTED, untouched,
  sha256=3a8621f721498eed104cbced963f30895a361f11d53193846acb6929b0f85910).
  Seeds: 1001, 1002, 1003 (none used during the original architecture search,
  which used seed=42 per eval_benchmark.py's hardcoded set_seed(42)).

Phase B molecules (never used during architecture search):
  - Ethanol  (C2H6O, 9 atoms)  split: data_cache/generalization_splits/md17_ethanol_split.npz
  - Aspirin  (C9H8O4, 21 atoms) split: data_cache/generalization_splits/md17_aspirin_split.npz
  Both splits use the same 950/50/1000 train/val/test convention as Uracil's
  protected split, random index-based partitioning of the full MD17 GDML
  trajectory, fixed disjoint train/val/test index sets (verified zero exact-
  geometry overlap across partitions, by direct coordinate-set intersection).
  Seed for Phase B runs: 42 (matches the original architecture-search seed,
  since Phase B's purpose is to test zero-tuning transfer, not seed variance).

