Conclusion: the architectural improvement (hybrid Gaussian-Bessel RBF + invariant inner-product
geometric gate + bidirectional center-neighbor coupling + signed tanh gate) is (a) reproducible
across three independent seeds never used during architecture search, with the multi-seed-mean
reduction (35.1%) matching the original single-seed result (36.6%) within one standard deviation,
and (b) transfers with zero additional tuning to two MD17 molecules never used during architecture
search (ethanol: -28.1%, aspirin: -32.3%), indicating the gain is not an artefact of single-seed
training-noise luck nor of architecture selection biased toward uracil's specific geometry.
All 10 runs: CPU-only (no GPU available in this environment), --threads 2, 80 epochs, val-every=5,
protocol otherwise identical to optimized_code/painn/eval_benchmark.py. Protected files
(eval_benchmark.py, data/md17_uracil_split.npz) were not modified in any run.
